## Original Content
Not every 46-year-old comedy still gets laughs, but Airplane! seems only to get funnier with the decades. Some viewers too young to have caught it in its theatrical release even take the&#160;Benjaminian view of it as the kind of great work that creates its own genre: the rapid-fire deadpan joke machine, we could call it. [&#8230;]

## Summary
The article discusses the enduring comedic appeal of the film 'Airplane!', which has become funnier over the decades. It highlights that even younger audiences who missed its original release view it as a genre-defining work characterized by rapid-fire deadpan humor.

## Key Points
- The comedy film 'Airplane!' remains humorous and relevant after more than 40 years.
- It is credited with creating a new sub-genre of comedy described as a 'rapid-fire deadpan joke machine'.
- The film is appreciated across generations, including viewers not present during its initial theatrical release.


